4. CRUD Operations

CRUD represents the four basic operations performed on data.

Operation	Meaning	SQL Command
C — Create	Add data	INSERT
R — Read	Retrieve data	SELECT
U — Update	Modify data	UPDATE
D — Delete	Remove data	DELETE
Examples
INSERT INTO Students
VALUES (101, 'Himani');

SELECT *
FROM Students;

UPDATE Students
SET Name = 'Poo'
WHERE ID = 101;

DELETE FROM Students
WHERE ID = 101;

Note: CREATE TABLE is a DDL operation. CRUD's "Create" operation is commonly performed using INSERT.

